{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Perq Supervisor — End-of-Turn Report (v3)",
  "version": "3.0.0",
  "description": "Reports the gate state at the end of each agent turn. INFORMATIONAL ONLY — never blocks anything. SCOPE: Perq Wallet project only — Step 0 short-circuits when the agent's last working directory is not inside Perq_Dev/. The blocking authority is `.kiro/hooks/perq-supervisor.kiro.hook` (preToolUse on `git push`). v3 adds the Perq-context guard. v2 mirrored the v4 supervisor's Gate 4B.7 (assertion density) and the SPOT-CHECK REQUIRED block emission.",
  "when": {
    "type": "agentStop"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "PERQ SUPERVISOR REPORTER (agentStop) v3 — end-of-turn gate report.\n\nREPORTING ONLY. Never deny. The blocking authority is the preToolUse hook on `git push`. This produces a single end-of-turn rollup so the user knows what state a push would be in.\n\n## Step 0 — verify Perq context (SCOPE GUARD — do this FIRST)\n\nThis reporter is scoped to the Perq Wallet project ONLY. It must NOT run gates when the agent's recent work was on unrelated projects.\n\nThe agent is in Perq context iff ANY of these holds:\n  (a) The most recent shell tool calls in this turn used `cwd` containing `/Perq_Dev` (substring match), OR\n  (b) The current Kiro workspace root resolves to `/Users/itsshail/Kiro-workspace/Perq_Dev`, OR\n  (c) `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` (run from any cwd touched this turn) returns a path ending in `/Perq_Dev` AND the file `.kiro/steering/perq.md` exists at that root\n\nIf NONE of those hold, respond with exactly one line:\n\n  REPORT: not in Perq context — supervisor scope is Perq_Dev only\n\nand stop. Do NOT run gates. Do NOT run `git status`, `npm test`, or any other command.\n\nIf the context check passes, continue to Step 1.\n\n## Step 1 — should I report?\n\nRun:\n  - `git status --porcelain`\n  - `git log @{u}.. --oneline 2>/dev/null`\n\nIf BOTH are empty (clean tree, fully pushed): output exactly one line and stop:\n\n  REPORT: no changes since last push — gates quiescent\n\nIf either is non-empty, continue.\n\n## Step 2 — pick the comparison baseline\n\n  (a) Working tree dirty, no unpushed commits → diff `HEAD` vs working tree. Use HEAD as baseline.\n  (b) Working tree clean, unpushed commits → diff `@{u}` vs HEAD. Use `@{u}` as baseline.\n  (c) Both → diff `@{u}` vs working tree. Use `@{u}` as baseline.\n\nUse the chosen baseline wherever the v4 preToolUse hook says `HEAD~1`.\n\n## Step 3 — run gates as a report\n\nRun the same gate sequence as `.kiro/hooks/perq-supervisor.kiro.hook` v4 (Gate 0 through Gate 5, including 4B.7) but capture status only — NEVER issue DENY or APPROVE.\n\nGates in order:\n  - Gate 0 — Spec exists for new fns. If a new `window.X = function` has no matching spec in `.kiro/specs/`, the report shows FAIL (not N/A).\n  - Gate 1 — `node --check preview-app.js`\n  - Gate 2 — `npm test`\n  - Gate 3 — `npm run test:smoke`\n  - Gate 4A.1 — cache buster (preview.html ?v=N advances if preview-app.js in diff)\n  - Gate 4A.2 — service worker version (N/A if no SW in repo)\n  - Gate 4A.3 — orphan asset references\n  - Gate 4B.1 — new globals referenced in tests\n  - Gate 4B.2 — edge case categories. If a new spec is in the diff, the report MUST also emit the SPOT-CHECK REQUIRED block defined below. The block appears in the report, not just on push.\n  - Gate 4B.3 — new test files wired into npm test + CI\n  - Gate 4B.4 — smoke ran (mirrors Gate 3)\n  - Gate 4B.5 — coverage floor ≥80% of new top-level fns\n  - Gate 4B.6 — TEST_RESULTS.md modified or contains today's UTC date\n  - Gate 4B.7 — assertion density. For every new test block in `scripts/perq-*-test.js`, confirm at least one of: `assert.`, `assertEqual`, `assertStrictEqual`, `expect(`, `throws(`, `rejects(`, `toThrow(`, comparison ops (`===`, `!==`, `>=`, `<=`, `>`, `<`), or `.includes(`, `.match(`, `.contains(`, `.toBe(`, `.toEqual(`, `.toHaveText(`, `.toHaveAttribute(`, `.toBeVisible(`, `.toBeHidden(`, `.toBeDefined(`. Trivial blocks fail this gate.\n  - Gate 5 — CHANGELOG entry (or `chore:`/`docs:`/`test:`/`ci:` exempt scope on the head commit)\n\n## Step 4 — SPOT-CHECK REQUIRED (mirror)\n\nIf a new spec is in the chosen diff (`<baseline> → working tree`), produce the SPOT-CHECK REQUIRED block exactly as the preToolUse hook does:\n\n  SPOT-CHECK REQUIRED:\n  Edge case: <name from spec § 5> → Test: <test path or test name> → Assertion: <exact line from test file>\n  Edge case: <name from spec § 5> → Test: <test path or test name> → Assertion: <exact line from test file>\n  ...\n\nOne row per declared edge case in § 5. If a case has no covering test, write `Test: NOT COVERED → Assertion: —`. The block does not block anything in the report — it surfaces what the human should eyeball before push.\n\n## Step 5 — produce the report\n\nOutput the same 15-row markdown table as the preToolUse hook (Gate 0 through 5 plus 4B.7). If 4B.2 fired, include the SPOT-CHECK REQUIRED block immediately after the table. Then a SUMMARY line. Then a single status line in this exact format:\n\nIf 0 fails:\n  REPORT: <N>/<N> gates pass — push will succeed\n\nIf >=1 fails:\n  REPORT: <N>/<M> gates pass, <K> failure(s) — push will be DENIED at preToolUse\n  Failed gates: <comma-separated list of gate IDs that failed>\n\nUse REPORT exclusively. Never use APPROVE or DENY (those are reserved for the blocking hook).\n\n## Notes — what this hook does NOT do\n\n- Does NOT block any tool call.\n- Does NOT modify any files. Reads git state, runs read-only test scripts, parses output.\n- Does NOT replace the preToolUse blocking gate. On `git push`, the preToolUse hook fires and produces its own table independently.\n- Tolerates ~10s overhead for `npm test` + `npm run test:smoke` — that is the cost-to-pay for moving from per-shell-call APPROVE noise to a single end-of-turn rollup."
  }
}
